					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13003629#post-4610310</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13003629/snippets-of-an-unveiled-world#post-4610310</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 23 Apr 2020 08:49:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>The Pighead</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3242824</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The non-serious answer : because I'm a devilish monster who wants to drink your tears and eradicate all joy in this Earth.</p> <p>The serious answer : because the music and the art cover of the CD smells Serpent's Hand vibes. Like, too much. Plus, don't forget that in the segment, I suggest that the members of the band know the Library and the anomalous since their early years as a band (so, since the end of the eighties). Which means that, technically, you can associate every Radiohead record since &quot;The Bends&quot; with the Hand.</p> <p>Yeah, except &quot;Pablo Honey&quot;. Again, he's forever alone, poor CD.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
